  <StreamGeometry x:Key="NutIconSettings">F1 M3,5.9 L21,5.9 L21,7.1 L3,7.1 Z M3,11.4 L21,11.4 L21,12.6 L3,12.6 Z M3,16.9 L21,16.9 L21,18.1 L3,18.1 Z M15.4,6.5 A2.6,2.6 0 1 1 15.39,6.5 Z M15.4,8 A1.1,1.1 0 1 0 15.41,8 Z M8.6,12 A2.6,2.6 0 1 1 8.59,12 Z M8.6,13.5 A1.1,1.1 0 1 0 8.61,13.5 Z M15.4,17.5 A2.6,2.6 0 1 1 15.39,17.5 Z M15.4,19 A1.1,1.1 0 1 0 15.41,19 Z</StreamGeometry>

  <!--
    ==================== Navigation glyphs (Fluent UI System Icons) ====================
    The five navigation silhouettes are the official 24px "regular" outlines from
    microsoft/fluentui-system-icons, imported verbatim and stored locally so the application stays
    offline. Source: https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-system-icons
    Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 Microsoft Corporation. See docs/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

    Fluent paths rely on the non-zero winding rule, hence the F1 prefix: their counters are cut by
    reversed sub-paths, so rendering them even-odd would fill the interiors and turn each glyph
    into a blob. Detail layers are drawn separately on top and never alter the base silhouette.
  -->
